s assume, could narrow the race in the final stretch.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Kim Reynolds (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's governor race is an open-seat contest now tilted toward Democrats. State Auditor Rob Sand, the Democratic nominee, holds a consistent polling lead over Republican Zach Lahn, with October surveys from Marist, YouGov, Emerson, SSRS, Suffolk, and Siena all showing him ahead by four to twelve points. Even polls with Republican sponsorship put Sand in front. The Gazette's editorial board has endorsed him, and prediction markets give him roughly an 86 to 88 percent chance of winning.\n\nThe state's six-point Republican lean and the absence of an incumbent on the ballot temper the expected margin, and open-seat races can tighten late. Still, with every recent survey, expert rating, and market pointing the same direction, Sand enters the final weeks as the clear favorite, while independent Sondra Wilson trails in the field.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8753, "margin": 5.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8859, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8669, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8657, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8472, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8297, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8592, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8769, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8877, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8875, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.895, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8938, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8853, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8878, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8885, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9358, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9281, "mar